body:
Looking at this PR again, I've considered the edge cases that blocked us from merging this in the past. These edge cases are actually already allowed, but our thinking was we'd want to make a decision on whether they should be allowed before we expand this to more cases.

```csharp
public partial class TestBase : Node
{
	public virtual string VirtualProperty { get; set; } = "Original virtual property";

	[Export]
	public virtual string ExportedVirtualProperty { get; set; } = "Original exported virtual property";

	[Export]
	public virtual string ExportedVirtualProperty2 { get; set; } = "Original exported virtual property 2";
}

public partial class TestDerived : TestBase
{
	[Export]
	public override string VirtualProperty { get; set; } = "Overridden virtual property";

	[Export]
	public override string ExportedVirtualProperty { get; set; } = "Overridden exported virtual property";

	public override string ExportedVirtualProperty2 { get; set; } = "Overridden exported virtual property";
}
```

- We mentioned re-exporting a property that was already exported in a base class should probably be disallowed.
- When overriding a property that is already exported by the base class, it's unclear which default value should win ("Original exported virtual property" -or- "Overridden exported virtual property"?)

This is what happens right today:

<img width="676" height="240" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9d0284b5-8a82-4932-9f7c-1dbc9d02f163" />

We can't look at GDScript for reference because it doesn't support overriding properties. Looking at `godot-cpp`, it allows you to re-export a property that was already exported in the same way that it happens right now with C#:

<img width="690" height="235" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/745cdd5b-8ffa-40a6-a9cf-30aec11107fa" />

The main difference between `godot-cpp` and C# is that the default value that wins is different. In C# the original wins, and in the `godot-cpp` the override wins.

We should probably change the default value that wins to align with `godot-cpp` since that's the behavior we'll get when we move to GDExtension. But otherwise, I no longer think this should be a blocker for merging this PR, so I'm approving but it needs to be rebased. Since I already rebased this PR to test it, feel free to take it from https://github.com/raulsntos/godot/commit/4bb041de8b6fa0b1bea889405fac773de0ce1bf9.
